# EVERY DOOR PART, ON ITS OWN — plan 17 `A8.9a`.
#
# ⚠ A COMPOSITE HIDES ITS PARTS, and this file exists because of it: with the
# opening profile on `door/frame` alone, the frame went 108 -> 300 vertices while
# the composed `door/hung` stayed at 108 and its picture said *nothing changed*.
# Only the element on its own showed the difference. So each part is opened and
# photographed by itself, and the assemblies after them.
#
#   node tools/script.mjs tools/scripts/doorparts.keys --port <p> --shots
#
# ⚠ CLOSE BEFORE OPENING — a server keeps its mode between runs and `44:<name>`
# refuses while a part is already open, so the previous subject's picture comes
# back under the new name with no error anyone reads.
# ⚠ AUTO, NOT EYES: a limb's mesh id is 8..15 and the client's `mesh_bit` answers
# the FIGURE's bit for every id at or below 15, so EYES hides a leaf with the body.

send 44:
at 0 0 0
verb raise
wait rebuilt
send 40:0
wait mode

echo --- the wall with a hole in it, and its head
send 44:door/frame
wait part 'door/frame' opened
at 0.0 -5.5 70
snap part-frame
snap part-frame
send 44:

echo --- the leaf, one timber panel
send 44:door/leaf
wait part 'door/leaf' opened
at -2.5 -2.5 35
snap part-leaf
snap part-leaf
send 44:

echo --- the gateway: two doorway edges, one arch across both
send 44:door/gateway
wait part 'door/gateway' opened
at 0.0 -6.0 70
snap part-gateway
snap part-gateway
send 44:

echo --- and the assemblies
send 44:door/hung
wait part 'door/hung' opened
at 0.0 -5.5 70
snap part-hung
snap part-hung
send 44:

send 44:door/gated
wait part 'door/gated' opened
at 0.0 -6.5 70
snap part-gated
snap part-gated
send 44:
